course: dictionary
lesson: 418
title: Learning a job: apprenticeship
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A word can be easier to understand when you read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «An apprenticeship means learning a job at work while being paid.» The clues are learning, job, work and paid, so an apprenticeship is training for a job that you do while you work.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Routes into computing include university, a time of training for a job while you work, courses and teaching yourself with projects.» The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The brackets in the sentence «Routes into computing include university, apprenticeships (working and learning at the same time), courses and teaching yourself with projects» are a clue too. The writer explains the word for you, which is a helpful kind of context.
fact: An apprenticeship is a time of training where you learn a trade or job by working with a skilled worker.
fact: An apprentice is often paid a small wage while they learn.
fact: Jobs you can learn through an apprenticeship include plumber, electrician, chef, hairdresser and engineer.
fact: «University» means studying a subject for a few years, while an apprenticeship means learning a job at work.
fact: Any period of learning a skill from someone more experienced can also be called an apprenticeship.
exercise: «An apprenticeship means learning a job at work while being paid.» What does apprenticeship mean? | A holiday at the seaside | *A time of training for a job, learned while working | A school trip to a museum | A test you take once at the end of school
exercise: Maya will start an apprenticeship as an electrician. What will she do? | *Learn the job by working with a skilled electrician | Write a book about electricity | Stay at home all year | Go to a sports camp for the summer
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Routes into computing include university, apprenticeships, courses and teaching yourself with projects» that names a way of learning a job while working. | *apprenticeships | courses | university | projects
test: Which of these could you learn through an apprenticeship? | *A plumber | A planet in space | A pancake | A cloud in the sky
test: «University means studying a subject for a few years.» How is an apprenticeship different? | *You learn a job at work while being paid | You study only at night in a library | You learn only by reading books | You never leave the house
exam: Which sentence shows someone doing an apprenticeship? | Ben plays football at the park | *Sam works with a skilled chef and learns to cook while being paid | Ella sits in a classroom reading about history | Jo goes to a museum on Saturday
